  "body": "## What changed\n- keep the current adaptive scaling logic while the calculated next step stays below the hard cap\n- when a later scaled step would exceed `maxAutomaticOffer`, clamp that step to the cap instead of ending the negotiation\n- allow subsequent configured steps to continue at the same capped price, preserving their step number, message, timing and reaction flow\n- keep the existing fail-closed behavior when the very first adaptive offer itself cannot fit under the hard cap\n- keep the safety rule that lowering the cap below an already-sent offer never generates a lower follow-up\n\n## Example\nWith a hard cap of 1350 PLN, a ladder that would scale to `1250 -> 1390 -> 1460` now becomes `1250 -> 1350 -> 1350` rather than stopping after step 1.\n\n## Tests\n- first adaptive offer still cannot cross the hard cap\n- later scaled steps clamp to the cap\n- later configured steps can remain at the same capped price\n- decision flow advances to the next configured step at the capped price\n- lowering the cap below an already-sent offer still stops automatic escalation",
